  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If \\(xy=a,\\) \\(xz=b,\\) and \\(yz=c,\\) and none of these quantities is \\(0,\\) then \\(x^2+y^2+z^2\\) equals",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{ab+ac+bc}{abc}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{a^2+b^2+c^2}{abc}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{(a+b+c)^2}{abc}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{(ab+ac+bc)^2}{abc}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{(ab)^2+(ac)^2+(bc)^2}{abc}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1983-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "From the three products, \\[ \\begin{aligned} x^2&=\\frac{ab}{c},\\\\ y^2&=\\frac{ac}{b},\\\\ z^2&=\\frac{bc}{a}. \\end{aligned} \\] Putting their sum over denominator \\(abc\\) gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} x^2+y^2+z^2 &=\\frac{(ab)^2+(ac)^2}{abc}\\\\ &\\quad+\\frac{(bc)^2}{abc}. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Multiply two of \\(xy=a,\\) \\(xz=b,\\) and \\(yz=c,\\) then divide by the third",
        "Use \\(x^2=\\frac{ab}{c},\\) \\(y^2=\\frac{ac}{b},\\) and \\(z^2=\\frac{bc}{a}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
